{
  "_meta": {
    "locales": "Four locales: en-us, en-ca, es-mx, fr-ca — the markets LC ships. ⚠️ ONLY en-us AND en-ca ARE REAL: es-mx and fr-ca carry the English copy verbatim as placeholders, so the keys exist for the copy team to fill and the table is never blank. Until they are translated those two markets read English, which is what getTrad's fallback would have done anyway — the difference is that a present key wins over the fallback, so these have to be overwritten rather than added. The one rule is never to leave a key as an empty string: the country key is matched before the fallback runs, so an empty fr-ca renders blank instead of falling through.",
    "source": "Figma \"LC_RBM Aperol - Luna\": desktop 5720:35673, compact 5720:35891. Row copy and cell copy are transcribed from the desktop frame's three product columns, left to right: Gen 2, Gen 3, Blayzer. Design tokens are in src/scss/variants/LC/_variables.scss; this file carries only content.",
    "figmaDeviations": "Two deliberate departures from the frame, both slips rather than choices. (1) The frame's meta-ai line for the third column reads \"MMAl AI not available (no camera)\" — capital i for a lowercase L, and the acronym doubled. Set to \"MMAI not available (no camera)\". (2) The frame gives all THREE columns the \"CAMERA + AUDIO\" badge, including the one whose every row says it has no camera: the instance was left at its default. The badge is omitted on Blayzer rather than authored as a contradiction.",
    "products": "THREE products, as the frame has them. Above two products the compact switcher appears instead of the \"only differences\" toggle, so family and shortName are populated on all three — they are what the switcher shows.",
    "productCodes": "products[].upc is the ONLY product field authored here: name fallback, packshot, price and the PDP link all come from the product service keyed by that UPC. VERIFIED 2026-09-21 against production on www.lenscrafters.com (store 10851) and www.lenscrafters.ca (store 10852): all three resolve on both. US: Gen 2 0RW4012 $379 (unavailable), Gen 3 0RW4011 $479, Blayzer 0RW7001 $499. Canada: Gen 2 CAD 519, Gen 3 CAD 599.",
    "productService": "LC is NOT on the service SGH uses — that path answers 404 here. It is on /AjaxPartNumberView, which needs a catalogId, nests its products at products.products.product[], returns listPrice as the literal \"$ 0\" and carries no ISO currency code. See src/js/variants/LC/product_service.js. Two consequences for authoring: there is never a struck-through price or a discount badge on this brand, and the currency is read from the page rather than the response.",
    "nameBadge": "products[].nameBadge is the pill beside the product name, and it is OPTIONAL. Populated it renders, omitted it emits no markup at all. It is a locale map like every other authored string, so it is per market too. It is NOT products[].badge, which is the line under the name with its icon. In the frame it sits on Blayzer, the new model. Authored in natural case, because the pill is uppercased in CSS.",
    "icons": "Icon values resolve against package.json > projectConfigurations.paths.productionImage, so the brand subfolder is part of the value — LC/, not SGH/. The svg files are byte-identical copies of the SGH ones, and they have to be copies: tasks/staticAsset.task.js excludes the other brands' folders from a build, so an LC json pointing at SGH/ would ship a broken icon.",
    "devOrigin": "comparison.api.devOrigin is development only and ignored in a production build: it is the storefront the CORS proxy (npm run proxy) is aimed at. Set to www.lenscrafters.com, which is verified answering. Point it at www.lenscrafters.ca to exercise the Canadian store and its CAD prices — note Canada is a separate DOMAIN on this brand, not a path."
  },
